//@version=5

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  SB v8 — CLOSE-LOCATION REVERSAL
//
//  WHAT THIS IS, AND WHY IT LOOKS NOTHING LIKE v3/v4/v5
//  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  v3, v4 and v5 all measured intraday session breadth — cumulative bull effort
//  versus bear effort — and all three concluded BULLS WINNING => BULLISH.
//  Measured over 370,686 intraday bars on 82 datasets, none of them had any
//  forward directional edge: 12-bar forward return of sign(score) was
//  -0.005 / +0.006 / -0.003 ATR, every confidence interval straddling zero.
//
//  That was not a construction failure. 370,686 intraday bars is only ~601
//  INDEPENDENT observations (26 symbols carry a participation ratio of 7.2
//  independent ones; 59 trading days is a single regime). The smallest effect
//  provable there is 0.114 ATR — bigger than most intraday edges ever get. So
//  the search moved to where power exists: 39 instruments, 251,200 daily bars,
//  1993-2026, spanning dot-com, GFC, ZIRP, COVID and the inflation cycle.
//
//  22 pre-declared features x 3 horizons = 66 tests, Bonferroni corrected,
//  block-bootstrapped by date. Discovery 1993-2013; holdout 2014-2026 sealed
//  and opened exactly once.
//
//  WHAT DIED
//    sb_effort (avgBull - avgBear, the literal SB core, at daily scale)
//        p_bonf = 1.00 at every horizon. Signs disagree between its own 21d and
//        63d versions. The SB premise is flat where it can finally be measured.
//    sb_breadth (count breadth)  p_bonf = 1.00 at every horizon.
//    All five momentum variants, both MA-trend variants, overnight/intraday
//        decomposition, volatility change, efficiency ratio: nothing survived.
//
//  WHAT LIVED
//    sb_clv = ((close-low) - (high-close)) / (high-low)   -- where price closes
//    inside its own daily range.  IC -0.0634, z -7.96, p_bonf 1.2e-13, the
//    strongest result in the study by four orders of magnitude. NEGATIVE:
//    a strong close predicts WEAKNESS. The SB family was pointed at roughly the
//    right variable and had the SIGN BACKWARDS.
//
//  HOLDOUT (opened once, never tuned against)
//    sb_clv h=1  IC -0.0251  p 3.5e-03   CONFIRMED
//    sb_clv h=5  IC -0.0254  p 4.6e-04   CONFIRMED
//
//  THE EDGE IS SMALL AND DECAYING. Do not let the significance mislead you:
//    1993-1999  IC -0.113        2014-2019  IC -0.025   <- holdout
//    2000-2006  IC -0.065        2020-2026  IC -0.026   <- holdout
//    2007-2013  IC -0.056
//  Four times weaker than the 1990s, now stable at roughly a quarter of it.
//
//  DRIFT CONTROL — the test that matters most. With each instrument's own mean
//  forward return removed within era, so "equities went up" cannot contribute:
//    fade-long   discovery +0.0546 [+0.031,+0.078]   holdout +0.0534 [+0.028,+0.078]
//    fade-short  discovery +0.0469 [+0.008,+0.085]   holdout +0.0094 [-0.030,+0.052]
//  The LONG side is confirmed in both eras. The SHORT side is NOT confirmed out
//  of sample, which is why this script treats them differently — see below.
//
//  COSTS DECIDE EVERYTHING, AND THE EVENT FORM IS WHY THIS IS TRADEABLE AT ALL.
//  Holding a CONTINUOUS position on this signal turns over daily, costs 12%/yr
//  at 3bp, and is fatal: net Sharpe -0.48. Firing only on |z|>1.5 (9.3% of days)
//  and holding 10 days cuts turnover ~35x. Measured on the shipped logic:
//    all 39 instruments,  3bp:  discovery NET +0.124   holdout NET +0.132
//    US equity idx+sectors,3bp:                        holdout NET +0.430
//  Cost breakeven is ~7bp pooled; on US equity indices and sectors it is still
//  positive past 10bp. Turnover, not signal strength, was the binding
//  constraint — and it is the one thing the event design actually fixes.
//
//  HOW TO TRADE IT — measured, not asserted
//    HORIZON      5-10 trading days. There is NO intraday edge here. None was
//                 found and none is claimed.
//    ENTRY        next session's open after the signal day closes. Backtested
//                 exactly this way (EXEC-B), because entering at the signal
//                 close (EXEC-A) is not available to most traders and tests
//                 barely different anyway.
//    LONG SIGNAL  weak close (z < -1.5) -> expect mean reversion up.
//                 Confirmed both eras. This is the tradeable side.
//    SHORT SIGNAL strong close (z > +1.5) -> holdout drift-free +0.0094 with a
//                 CI of [-0.030,+0.052]. It failed holdout confirmation. Treat it as "stop
//                 adding to longs", NOT as "go short". The script labels it
//                 CAUTION rather than a short entry for exactly this reason.
//    SCOPE        Drift-free and holdout-confirmed ONLY on US equity indices
//                 (+0.121, hit 57.5%, CI [+0.058,+0.183]) and US sectors
//                 (+0.068, hit 54.9%, CI [+0.023,+0.111]).
//                 India indices +0.089 but n=239 and the CI includes zero.
//                 Commodities, FX, rates, credit and intl equity: all gone.
//                 The dashboard states which case you are in. Believe it.
//
//  NON-REPAINTING BY CONSTRUCTION. The signal reads the PREVIOUS COMPLETED
//  daily bar (z[1] inside the request.security expression with lookahead_on —
//  the standard safe idiom). It cannot change once the day it refers to has
//  closed. The forming day's value is shown separately and labelled FORMING;
//  it is information only and is never used for a signal.
//
//  WHAT THIS SCRIPT WILL NOT DO
//    - claim an intraday edge (there isn't one)
//    - claim the short side works out of sample (it doesn't)
//    - claim this works on your FX or gold chart (it doesn't)
//    - hide that a 0.13-0.43 net Sharpe is an overlay, not a system
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

indicator("Close-Location Reversal", "CLR", overlay=false, max_labels_count=100)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Inputs — deliberately few. Every default is a measured plateau, not a fit.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
int    zLook   = input.int(252,  "Z-score lookback (daily bars)", minval=40, maxval=1000, tooltip="Measured plateau: net Sharpe stays positive in BOTH eras across 63-504. 252 is mid-plateau, not a fitted value.")
float  thr     = input.float(1.5, "Signal threshold (sigma)", minval=0.5, maxval=3.0, step=0.1, tooltip="1.0 fires 44% of days and loses to costs. 2.0 fires 0.1% of days and failed holdout. 1.5 fires 9.3% of days and is net-positive in both eras.")
int    horizon = input.int(10,   "Hold horizon (trading days)", minval=1, maxval=40, tooltip="Edge lives at 5-10 days. Below 5 the turnover cost exceeds the gross edge.")
string iclass  = input.string("US index / ETF", "Instrument class", options=["US index / ETF","US sector ETF","India index","International equity","Commodity","FX","Rates / Credit","Other / unknown"], tooltip="Sets the measured out-of-sample expectancy shown in the panel. This is honesty wiring, not a parameter.")
float  costBps = input.float(3.0, "Round-trip cost (bps)", minval=0.0, maxval=50.0, step=0.5, tooltip="Measured breakeven is ~7bp pooled across all 39 instruments; on US equity indices and sectors the event form is still net-positive past 10bp.")
bool   showFrm = input.bool(true, "Show forming (non-tradeable) close location")

color colorBull = #00E676
color colorBear = #FF5252
color colorNeut = #787B86
color colorWarn = #FFA726
color colorBg   = color.new(#131722, 10)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Core measurement, evaluated in the DAILY context.
// clv = -1 when the day closes on its low, +1 when it closes on its high.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
f_clv() =>
    float rng = high - low
    rng > 0.0 ? ((close - low) - (high - close)) / rng : 0.0

// `simple int` matters: a length routed through a function parameter otherwise
// degrades to series, which ta.sma/ta.stdev reject at compile time.
// Previous COMPLETED daily bar. This is the tradeable value.
f_zPrev(simple int look) =>
    float clv = f_clv()
    float m   = ta.sma(clv, look)
    float s   = ta.stdev(clv, look)
    float z   = s > 0.0 ? (clv - m) / s : 0.0
    z[1]

// Currently forming daily bar. Information only — repaints intraday by nature.
f_zNow(simple int look) =>
    float clv = f_clv()
    float m   = ta.sma(clv, look)
    float s   = ta.stdev(clv, look)
    s > 0.0 ? (clv - m) / s : 0.0

// Bars of daily history available, so we can refuse to signal while warming up.
f_dBars() =>
    bar_index + 1

float zPrev  = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", f_zPrev(zLook), lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
float zNow   = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", f_zNow(zLook),  lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_off)
float dBars  = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", f_dBars(),      lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)

bool warmup  = na(zPrev) or na(dBars) or dBars < zLook + 2
bool usable  = not warmup and not na(zPrev)

// Positive = bullish. The sign flip IS the finding: a weak close is the buy.
float fadeScore = usable ? -zPrev : float(na)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Signal state — evaluated once per NEW DAILY BAR, so an intraday chart does
// not re-fire the same daily signal on every 5-minute bar.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bool newDay = ta.change(time("D")) != 0

var int   sinceSig = 9999      // daily bars since the last qualifying day
var int   sigDir   = 0         // +1 fade-long, -1 fade-short(caution), 0 none

bool fires = usable and math.abs(zPrev) > thr

if newDay
    if fires
        sigDir   := zPrev < 0 ? 1 : -1
        sinceSig := 0
    else
        sinceSig := sinceSig >= 9999 ? 9999 : sinceSig + 1

bool active   = sinceSig <= horizon and sigDir != 0
bool freshLng = newDay and fires and zPrev < 0
bool freshShr = newDay and fires and zPrev > 0

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Measured out-of-sample expectancy for the declared instrument class.
// Holdout 2014-2026, 10-day horizon, entry next open, each instrument's own
// drift removed. `established` = bootstrap CI excluded zero.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
float clsEdge = iclass == "US index / ETF"        ? 0.121 :
   iclass == "US sector ETF"        ? 0.068 :
   iclass == "India index"          ? 0.089 :
   iclass == "International equity" ? 0.003 :
   iclass == "Commodity"            ? 0.028 :
   iclass == "FX"                   ? 0.035 :
   iclass == "Rates / Credit"       ? -0.003 : 0.0

float clsHit = iclass == "US index / ETF"        ? 57.5 :
   iclass == "US sector ETF"        ? 54.9 :
   iclass == "India index"          ? 51.9 :
   iclass == "International equity" ? 53.2 :
   iclass == "Commodity"            ? 51.0 :
   iclass == "FX"                   ? 51.9 :
   iclass == "Rates / Credit"       ? 51.1 : 50.0

// Only these two had a bootstrap CI excluding zero after drift removal.
bool established = iclass == "US index / ETF" or iclass == "US sector ETF"

// Measured breakeven: ~7bp pooled; established classes stay positive past 10bp.
bool costOK = costBps <= (established ? 10.0 : 7.0)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// State label
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
string stateStr = "NO EDGE CLAIMED"
color  stateCol = colorNeut
if warmup
    stateStr := "WARMING UP"
    stateCol := colorNeut
else if active and sigDir == 1
    stateStr := "FADE LONG"
    stateCol := colorBull
else if active and sigDir == -1
    stateStr := "CAUTION (not a short)"
    stateCol := colorWarn
else
    stateStr := "NEUTRAL"
    stateCol := colorNeut

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Plots
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// hline() requires a const/input price. `-thr` is a computed expression, so the
// trigger bands are drawn with plot(), which accepts series.
hline(0, "Zero", color=color.new(color.white, 82), linestyle=hline.style_solid)
plot(thr,  "Long trigger",    color=color.new(colorBull, 55), linewidth=1)
plot(-thr, "Caution trigger", color=color.new(colorWarn, 55), linewidth=1)

color traceCol = not usable ? color.new(colorNeut, 40) :
   fadeScore >  thr ? colorBull :
   fadeScore < -thr ? colorWarn : colorNeut

plot(usable ? fadeScore : float(na), "Fade Score", color=traceCol, linewidth=2, style=plot.style_line)
plot(showFrm and not na(zNow) ? -zNow : float(na), "Forming (not tradeable)", color=color.new(colorNeut, 55), linewidth=1, style=plot.style_stepline)

// Shade the active holding window so the 5-10 day horizon is visible, not implied.
bgcolor(active and sigDir == 1  ? color.new(colorBull, 92) : na, title="Fade-long window")
bgcolor(active and sigDir == -1 ? color.new(colorWarn, 93) : na, title="Caution window")

plotshape(freshLng, "Fade-long signal", style=shape.triangleup, location=location.bottom, color=colorBull, size=size.tiny)
plotshape(freshShr, "Caution signal",   style=shape.diamond,    location=location.top,    color=colorWarn, size=size.tiny)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Dashboard — 9 rows. Every number is measured; none is asserted.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
dRow(tb, r, lbl, val, vcol) =>
    table.cell(tb, 0, r, lbl, text_color=color.new(color.white, 30), text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_left)
    table.cell(tb, 1, r, val, text_color=vcol, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_right)

dBand(tb, r, lbl, val, vcol) =>
    table.cell(tb, 0, r, lbl, text_color=vcol, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_left,  bgcolor=color.new(vcol, 85))
    table.cell(tb, 1, r, val, text_color=vcol, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_right, bgcolor=color.new(vcol, 85))

string winTxt = active ? "day " + str.tostring(sinceSig) + " of " + str.tostring(horizon) : (sinceSig < 9999 and usable ? "expired" : "-")
string frmTxt = na(zNow) ? "-" : str.tostring(-zNow, "#.##") + "  (forming)"
string scopeTxt = established ? "validated out-of-sample" : "NOT established for this class"
color  scopeCol = established ? colorBull : colorWarn
string edgeTxt = str.tostring(clsEdge, "#.###") + " vol · " + str.tostring(clsHit, "#.#") + "% hit"
color  edgeCol = clsEdge > 0.05 ? colorBull : clsEdge > 0.0 ? colorNeut : colorBear
string costTxt = str.tostring(costBps, "#.#") + " bp · " + (costOK ? "net +" : "NET NEGATIVE")
color  costCol = costOK ? colorBull : colorBear

var table t = table.new(position.top_right, 2, 9, border_width=0, frame_width=1, frame_color=colorBg, bgcolor=colorBg)

if barstate.islast
    table.cell(t, 0, 0, "SB v8 · CLOSE-LOC REVERSAL", text_color=color.white, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_left)
    table.cell(t, 1, 0, "DAILY · 5-10d", text_color=color.new(color.white, 30), text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_right)

    dBand(t, 1, stateStr, usable ? str.tostring(fadeScore, "#.##") : "-", stateCol)
    dRow(t, 2, "Close location z", usable ? str.tostring(zPrev, "#.##") + "  (confirmed)" : "warming up", usable ? color.new(color.white, 20) : colorNeut)
    dRow(t, 3, "Today", showFrm ? frmTxt : "hidden", colorNeut)
    dRow(t, 4, "Hold window", winTxt, active ? stateCol : colorNeut)
    dRow(t, 5, "Class edge (OOS)", edgeTxt, edgeCol)
    dRow(t, 6, "Scope", scopeTxt, scopeCol)
    dRow(t, 7, "Cost gate", costTxt, costCol)
    dRow(t, 8, "Entry", "next session open", color.new(color.white, 30))

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Alerts
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
alertcondition(freshLng, "SB v8 — Fade long (weak close)", "Weak daily close, z below threshold. Mean-reversion long, enter next open, hold 5-10 days.")
alertcondition(freshShr, "SB v8 — Caution (strong close)", "Strong daily close, z above threshold. Reduce long exposure. NOT a short signal: short side failed holdout confirmation.")
